          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", both a "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "; "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·10",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·12",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", both a "
        },
        {
          "text": "b7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "; and "
        },
        {
          "text": "4·12",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", another "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". Those five are this chapter's whole subject, and the next lesson is where they get a fingering."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That's also why this chapter opens where it does. Strict C-A-G-E-D order sends the C form first — the highest of the five windows and, as chapter 2 found, the least friendly to a whole hand. Same order, same reasoning as before. Explore any window with root "
        },
        {
          "text": "A",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " in the "
        },
        {
          "text": "Scale Visualizer",
          "link": {
            "kind": "screen",
            "href": "/scale-visualizer"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", or go straight to "
        },
        {
          "text": "the C form",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "minor-caged-pentatonic-c-form"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " and the first of the two windows that spread."
        }
      ]
